    <string name="import_purpose">Keep the original subscription and produce a normalized mihomo document plus an offline node list.</string>
    <string name="import_scenarios">Use a URL or pasted text to import native YAML, supported Surge profiles or node URI lists, including supported Base64 subscriptions.</string>
    <string name="import_cautions">Imports are limited to 4 MiB. Documents may contain credentials and remain in app-private storage. Unsupported formats are rejected; partial conversions report skipped nodes. Closing help preserves your draft. An empty name uses Profile-Title (including Base64) or the name in Subscription-Userinfo, then numbered unnamed subscriptions. Conversion runs before the associated script or local configuration.</string>
    <string name="mode_purpose">Choose the final runtime mode: rule, global or direct.</string>
    <string name="mode_scenarios">Rule follows configured rules. Global uses the global policy. Direct bypasses proxy policies.</string>
    <string name="mode_cautions">Home always injects this choice after subscription and local processing. Restart VPN to use a changed mode.</string>
    <string name="config_purpose">Compose a subscription with a sparse set of local overrides while retaining unknown subscription fields.</string>
    <string name="config_scenarios">Create local configuration, scripts, proxy groups or routing rules, then associate them with a subscription and preview the composed result.</string>
    <string name="config_cautions">Only enabled fields are emitted. The original, composed candidate and active core configuration are separate states. A successful preview does not mean VPN is connected.</string>
